# The bus request/response idiom: query and source-addressed result [SPEC:CXC-BUS-QUERY]

> **[PLACEMENT UNRATIFIED].** Written into `corpora/platform-specs/` because that is where its
> neighbours live (`82-document-store-containment.lts`, `83-print-services.lts`), not because the
> placement was ruled — see [CXC-VISION-PLACEMENT] for the standing note on this directory's
> unratified filename numbering. Filename `86-composebus-request-response.lts` is the first
> non-colliding slot after `85-composeserver-plugin-contract.lts`; provisional. Placed here rather
> than in the (currently empty) `document-store` corpus deliberately: David's dispatch named this as
> the platform's FIRST request/response idiom that other query services will copy, so the reusable
> PATTERN belongs at platform scope with document_store as its first application — not filed as if
> it were document_store-only. If the `document-store` corpus is later populated as document_store's
> own spec home, [CXC-BUS-QUERY-DOCSTORE] (the application, not the pattern) is the node most likely
> to move there; [CXC-BUS-QUERY-IDIOM]/[-ORDERING]/[-VALIDATION] should stay platform-level regardless.

