## [DEC-DOCSTORE-BUS-QUERY-FACE] Decision — document_store gets a bus query face, additive to HTTP

- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-BUS-QUERY]
- lifecycle-position: decided
- provenance: david-ruling
- dsd-source: docs/composeserver/DECISIONS-phase1-plan.md
- dsd-decision: D3
- decision: build the `_doc/*/query -> _doc/*/result/{src}` request/response idiom as the platform's reference pattern; document_store's blob and external-client surface stays on HTTP. Bus query face is ADDITIVE, not a replacement.
- rationale: David ratified Phase-1 DSD D3 (see `[DEC-PHASE1-DSD-CALLS-SETTLED]`) accepting the architect's recommendation over the two alternatives offered — bus-only (forces every current HTTP client, e.g. `resolve.py`, to migrate at once; risk to a live ~27-day dependency) and leave-HTTP-only (no new vocabulary, but document_store never becomes a bus peer). "Bus query face + keep HTTP" was lean, additive, and low-risk to a live service, and it is the option that actually establishes the reference idiom other query services need to copy — the other two either force a risky migration or never produce the vocabulary at all.
- dsd-text: "**Why it matters:** it introduces the platform's first **request/response** namespace idiom (a query namespace answered on a per-source result namespace) — a vocabulary decision that other query services will copy."
- alternatives-rejected: bus-only (D3 option table, rejected — forces `resolve.py` and other live HTTP clients to migrate at once); leave-HTTP-only (rejected — no new vocabulary, document_store never joins the bus).
- see-also: [SPEC:CXC-BUS-QUERY], [CXC-BUS-QUERY-DOCSTORE]

